From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lenOS hardening <hardening@lenos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: trigger GC on keyguard lock (memory-clear-on-lock)

This is the SystemUI half of the memory-clear-on-lock feature (GrapheneOS
release 2024020500: "run full compacting garbage collection ... in SystemUI
and system_server after locking"). The system_server half is fwb-0002
(KeyguardStateMonitor).

When KeyguardViewMediator transitions to showing=true (the keyguard locks),
request a concurrent GC in the SystemUI process so freed pages holding
PIN/password-derived secrets are returned to the kernel and zeroed by the
GKI base's init-on-alloc page zeroing.

Uses VMRuntime.requestConcurrentGC() (public API, Android 12+). The
full-compacting variant GrapheneOS describes uses a hidden ART API we do not
call; requestConcurrentGC is the safe, verifiable approximation.

Pairs with: fwb-0002 (system_server), and requires the kernel init-on-alloc
zeroing that the sm7635 GKI base already enables (lenos_standard.config).
---
diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/KeyguardViewMediator.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/KeyguardViewMediator.java
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/KeyguardViewMediator.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/KeyguardViewMediator.java
@@ -113,6 +113,8 @@
 import androidx.annotation.Nullable;
 import androidx.annotation.VisibleForTesting;
 
+import dalvik.system.VMRuntime;
+
 import com.android.app.animation.Interpolators;
 import com.android.app.tracing.coroutines.TrackTracer;
 import com.android.internal.jank.InteractionJankMonitor;
@@ -4249,9 +4251,21 @@
         final boolean notifyDefaultDisplayCallbacks = showing != mShowing || forceCallbacks;
         final boolean updateActivityLockScreenState = showing != mShowing
                 || aodShowing != mAodShowing || forceCallbacks;
+        final boolean wasShowing = mShowing;
         mShowing = showing;
         mAodShowing = aodShowing;
 
+        if (showing && !wasShowing) {
+            // lenOS: purge PIN/password-derived data from SystemUI memory when the
+            // keyguard shows (device locks). Combined with the GKI base's init-on-alloc
+            // page zeroing, a GC returns freed pages to the kernel and zeroes them.
+            // This is the SystemUI half of GrapheneOS release 2024020500 (full GC in
+            // system_server AND SystemUI on lock); the system_server half is
+            // KeyguardStateMonitor (fwb-0002). requestConcurrentGC() is public API
+            // since Android 12.
+            VMRuntime.getRuntime().requestConcurrentGC();
+        }
+
         if (updateActivityLockScreenState) {
             updateActivityLockScreenState(showing, aodShowing, reason);
         }
